{"step_index":127,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T12:49:56Z","input_tokens":8691,"cache_read_tokens":176608,"output_tokens":3162,"thinking":"Analyzing `SerialiseChannel` function, specifically how it processes an `sNVChannel*` structure. This structure's location within the `Recipients` data, starting at an offset, is critical. The function's memory write pattern to the output buffer is the primary point of interest. Further investigation needed to understand the data being serialized.\n\n\nInitial hypothesis: offsets within `sNVChannel` are derived from the Recipient's access pattern relative to the channel base. The relationship is OFFSET - 0x89C. `SerialiseChannel`'s operation involves a direct memory mapping from an in-memory offset, relative to `rbx` (which is within `sNVChannel`), to a disk offset. Tracing the first 13 bytes of `SerialiseChannel`, the function appears to copy `rbx + 0x00 .. 0x0C` to `r11 + 0x00 .. 0x0C`. The data at `sNVData + 0x89C + 0x00 .. 0x0C` corresponds to this block.\n\n\nThe first 6 bytes at `r11 + 0x00 .. 0x05` represent the channel name. The channel name is 6 ASCII characters, likely null-padded, as confirmed by a prior dialog's length restriction. Byte at `r11 + 0x0C` corresponds to the channel color, matching the `NameAndColorRecipient` structure. Further, the preamp setting is found at `r11 + 0x34` (uint16), with a default of 100.\n\n\nAnalyzing the memory offsets within `SerialiseChannel`, focusing on how they relate to the `HighLowPassFilterRecipient` and `GateRecipient` structures. Observed that the HPF frequency is located at `r11 + 0x54` (uint16) and `r11 + 0x56` and `r11 + 0x57` are likely HPF In/Out settings. The gate-related data is starting at the offset `r11 + 0x5C`. Additional analysis needed for gate-specific parameters.\n\n\nThe offset `0x8FC` relative to the channel base translates to an offset of `0x60`, suggesting a connection between memory locations in the data file. Observed data at offset `+0x05C` in `SQ5.DAT`.\n\nNow examining the PEQ 4-Band parameters serialized by `SerialiseChannel`. The function at `0x0E36CA` is called with arguments derived from `rbx + 0x80` and `r11 + 0x7C`, corresponding to `SQ5.DAT +0x07C`. Each band's parameters (gain, frequency, width) are extracted from specific offsets within this region. Compressor settings are located starting at offset `r11 + 0xF4`. The function at `0x0E370D` is called to serialize them.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$bytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes(\"C:\\Program Files\\Allen & Heath\\SQ MixPad 1.6.1\\SQ MixPad.exe\")\nfunction DumpHex($title, $start, $end) {\n    Write-Host \"=== $title (0x$($start.ToString('X6')) .. 0x$($end.ToString('X6'))) ===\"\n    for ($p = $start; $p -lt $end; $p += 16) {\n        $hex = ($bytes[$p..($p+15)] | ForEach-Object { $_.ToString(\"X2\") }) -join \" \"\n        Write-Host (\"0x{0:X6}: {1}\" -f $p, $hex)\n    }\n}\nDumpHex \"Gate Serialise (0x0E33D0..0x0E3460)\" 0x0E33D0 0x0E3460\nDumpHex \"PEQ Serialise (0x0E26D0..0x0E2780)\" 0x0E26D0 0x0E2780\nDumpHex \"Comp Serialise (0x0E3150..0x0E3260)\" 0x0E3150 0x0E3260\nDumpHex \"Main SerialiseScene (0x0E2160..0x0E26D0)\" 0x0E2160 0x0E26D0","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Dump Gate, PEQ, Comp, and Scene serializer functions in SQ MixPad.exe"}}]}
